# 4. User Roles

## Customer

Customer should be able to:

- Register/login
- Allow location access
- Select delivery location
- Discover nearby merchants
- Search products
- Browse merchant catalogue/menu
- Add products to cart
- Select merchant delivery / partner delivery / pickup
- Place order
- Pay online or COD where supported
- Track order
- Track rider
- Receive notifications
- View order history
- Raise support/refund request

---

## Merchant

Merchant should be able to:

- Register business
- Upload documents
- Wait for admin approval
- Login securely
- Add/edit products
- Add product images
- Change price
- Change stock
- Enable/disable product
- Set store timings
- Set store location
- Set delivery radius
- Enable own delivery
- Accept/reject orders
- Confirm availability
- Mark preparing
- Mark ready
- Hand over to rider
- View completed orders
- View settlement/payment information

Merchant confirmation is part of the intended OWNLOCAL LIVE order flow.

---

## Delivery Partner

Rider should be able to:

- Register
- Upload ID/license/vehicle details
- Wait for admin approval
- Login
- Go online/offline
- Share GPS while active
- See nearby delivery jobs
- Accept/decline job
- See pickup merchant
- Navigate to merchant
- Confirm pickup
- Navigate to customer
- Complete delivery using OTP
- View earnings
- View delivery history

Do not expose unrestricted customer address/contact information before rider assignment.

---

## Admin

Admin should be web-first.

Admin should handle:

- Merchant approvals
- Rider approvals
- Customer support
- Orders
- Refunds
- Payment reconciliation
- Merchant documents
- Rider documents
- Complaints
- Block/unblock accounts
- Audit logs
- Suspicious activity
- Reports
- Configuration

The source project explicitly calls for role-limited access and protection of identity documents, phone numbers, bank details and customer addresses.

